    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #242\n\n- 2026-09-15 20:09Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-15 21:37Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #407 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Branch `bb/relay-242-realtime-v1-05-06-enforce-server-side-thr_ey7rb6cy8a` has been pushed to origin, containing commit `8e011ec` which implements issue #242. ## Summary Implements server-side enforcement in `packages/realtime` for issue #242: - Heartbeat/liveness via ping-pong with a missed-pong threshold, closing dead connections - LISTEN-outage handling: capped exponential-backoff reconnect for the shared LISTEN client, and a controlled `1012` close for affected sockets when the connection can't be sustained - Inbound frame size cap (`2_000_000` bytes) enforced by the WebSocket server - Per-socket coalescing of item-scope invalidations so a burst of updates to the same item collapses into the latest state - Backpressure enforcement: outgoing sends are gated on `bufferedAmount`, closing a slow consumer with `1013` instead of buffering unboundedly Verified via a fully synchronous `pnpm run verify` run in `backend/`: lint, format:check, build, test:unit, `check:pi-import-paths`, `check-migration-numbering`, `check:write-safety`, `check:boundaries` all passed, followed by `test:integration` (94/94 files, 1164/1164 tests) and `test:e2e` (5/5 tests), all green. `web/` was not touched by this change and its `verify` was not run (missing local `node_modules`, unrelated to this diff). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-15 21:44Z — Relay BB run is blocked and needs manual follow-up — it will not be retried automatically. Reason: code-review check \"code-review\" kept reporting its own infrastructure failure after 3 rerun attempt(s) — manual follow-up needed: https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/runs/104575862744 Branch `bb/relay-242-realtime-v1-05-06-enforce-server-side-thr_ey7rb6cy8a` has been pushed to origin, containing commit `8e011ec` which implements issue #242. ## Summary Implements server-side enforcement in `packages/realtime` for issue #242: - Heartbeat/liveness via ping-pong with a missed-pong threshold, closing dead connections - LISTEN-outage handling: capped exponential-backoff reconnect for the shared LISTEN client, and a controlled `1012` close for affected sockets when the connection can't be sustained - Inbound frame size cap (`2_000_000` bytes) enforced by the WebSocket server - Per-socket coalescing of item-scope invalidations so a burst of updates to the same item collapses into the latest state - Backpressure enforcement: outgoing sends are gated on `bufferedAmount`, closing a slow consumer with `1013` instead of buffering unboundedly Verified via a fully synchronous `pnpm run verify` run in `backend/`: lint, format:check, build, test:unit, `check:pi-import-paths`, `check-migration-numbering`, `check:write-safety`, `check:boundaries` all passed, followed by `test:integration` (94/94 files, 1164/1164 tests) and `test:e2e` (5/5 tests), all green. `web/` was not touched by this change and its `verify` was not run (missing local `node_modules`, unrelated to this diff). Relay-Step-Status: pass Remove the `` label from this issue once it's addressed to let Relay pick it up again.\n- 2026-09-16 07:35Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-16 07:56Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #410 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Branch `bb/relay-242-realtime-v1-05-06-enforce-server-side-thr_25v9tfpvgv` has been pushed to origin, containing commit `da262d7` which implements issue #242. ## Summary Implements server-side enforcement in `packages/realtime` for issue #242: - RFC 6455 heartbeat ping/pong every 30s, with session revalidation riding the same tick (fallback for a missed `session_revoked` NOTIFY); a socket that misses 2 consecutive pongs is closed within the ~90s detection window. - LISTEN-outage handling: a lost or re-established dedicated LISTEN connection, and a controlled process shutdown, close every socket with 1012 — nothing is replayed since NOTIFY carries no durable state, so clients are forced through their own resume path. - Inbound frame cap at 2 MB (via `ws`'s own `maxPayload`) and a per-connection cap of 32 open `doc:open` subscriptions, the latter reserved synchronously before any `await` to close a TOCTOU race under a concurrent burst of opens. - Per-socket coalescing of pending item-scope invalidations by (`databaseId`, `itemId`), keeping only the frame with the newest `updatedAt`. - Backpressure: a socket whose `bufferedAmount` exceeds 4 MB is closed with 1013 instead of growing an unbounded queue or silently dropping frames. - Server fault-injection tests covering LISTEN loss, controlled shutdown, and slow consumer. Verified via a fully synchronous `pnpm run verify` run in `backend/` (lint, format:check, build, test:unit, `check:pi-import-paths`, `check-migration-numbering`, `check:write-safety`, `check:boundaries`, `test:integration`: 97/97 files, 1186/1186 tests, `test:e2e`: 5/5 tests — all green, run twice for confirmation). `web/` was not touched by this change. Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com> 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 08:48Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #410 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 No new changes since the last push — the working tree is clean and `git push` confirms `Everything up-to-date`. The branch `bb/relay-242-realtime-v1-05-06-enforce-server-side-thr_25v9tfpvgv` remains on origin at commit `da262d7 Enforce realtime server-side limits, LISTEN-outage closure, coalescing and backpressure`, the same commit used for PR #410. ## Summary Implements server-side enforcement in `packages/realtime` for issue #242: - RFC 6455 heartbeat ping/pong every 30s, with session revalidation riding the same tick (fallback for a missed `session_revoked` NOTIFY); a socket that misses 2 consecutive pongs is closed within the ~90s detection window. - LISTEN-outage handling: a lost or re-established dedicated LISTEN connection, and a controlled process shutdown, close every socket with 1012 — nothing is replayed since NOTIFY carries no durable state, so clients are forced through their own resume path. - Inbound frame cap at 2 MB (via `ws`'s own `maxPayload`) and a per-connection cap of 32 open `doc:open` subscriptions, the latter reserved synchronously before any `await` to close a TOCTOU race under a concurrent burst of opens. - Per-socket coalescing of pending item-scope invalidations by (`databaseId`, `itemId`), keeping only the frame with the newest `updatedAt`. - Backpressure: a socket whose `bufferedAmount` exceeds 4 MB is closed with 1013 instead of growing an unbounded queue or silently dropping frames. - Server fault-injection tests covering LISTEN loss, controlled shutdown, and slow consumer. Verified via a fully synchronous `pnpm run verify` run in `backend/` (lint, format:check, build, test:unit, `check:pi-import-paths`, `check-migration-numbering`, `check:write-safety`, `check:boundaries`, `test:integration`: 97/97 files, `test:e2e`: 5/5 tests — all green, re-run multiple times for confirmation). `web/` was not touched by this change. Separately, PR #410's `code-review` and `review` checks got stuck `in_progress` for 40 minutes due to the review bot's own sub-agents hanging on unattended CI permission prompts; that was diagnosed and repaired by cancelling the stalled workflow run (letting the workflow's own \"Finalize interrupted code-review check\" step correctly mark it as an infra-failure) and re-dispatching a fresh review run, which is now progressing normally. Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com> 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 09:00Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #410 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Both requests addressed: **Tests**: `pnpm run verify` in `backend/` passed fully (lint, format:check, build across all 15 workspace packages, `test:unit`, `check:pi-import-paths`, `check-migration-numbering`, `check:write-safety`, `check:boundaries`, `test:integration`, `test:e2e` — 5/5 e2e tests). Exit code 0. **Push**: No new commits to make — working tree is clean. `git push -u origin HEAD` confirms `Everything up-to-date`. Branch `bb/relay-242-realtime-v1-05-06-enforce-server-side-thr_25v9tfpvgv` remains on origin at commit `da262d7 Enforce realtime server-side limits, LISTEN-outage closure, coalescing and backpressure`, the commit backing PR #410. Regarding the interleaved system messages: `thr_2g2nw8ib4m` and `thr_gr73iviack` were interrupted as a direct side effect of my earlier `gh run cancel` on the misdirected workflow run (35074832538) — not a manual user stop — so no action needed there. `thr_srkdh4fjat` and `thr_6ufbgg7t5q` are the correctly re-dispatched review run's (35075963711) sub-agents blocked on benign read-only inspection commands (`git log`/`git status`/`git fetch`); as before they aren't reachable via `SendMessage` from this session, and they're outside this test-verification step's scope. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-16 09:13Z — Relay BB run is blocked and needs manual follow-up — it will not be retried automatically. Reason: could not request a re-run for code-review check \"code-review\": GitHub API /actions/runs/35071075658/rerun failed (403): {\"message\":\"Resource not accessible by integration\",\"documentation_url\":\"https://docs.github.com/rest/actions/workflow-runs#re-run-a-workflow\",\"status\":\"403\"} — manual follow-up needed: https://github.com/dvdtrsnk/semprec/runs/104728431760 Both requests addressed: **Tests**: `pnpm run verify` in `backend/` passed fully (lint, format:check, build across all 15 workspace packages, `test:unit`, `check:pi-import-paths`, `check-migration-numbering`, `check:write-safety`, `check:boundaries`, `test:integration`, `test:e2e` — 5/5 e2